Log for major changes in releases


v4.0.0 (Not yet released) — BREAKS COMPATIBILITY, READ NOTES
----------------------------------------------------
- Cleanup release. See RELEASE_NOTES for details.

Removed (breaking)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
- `utils.convert_corr`: removed the `convertTo` keyword. It was
  renamed to `convert_to` in v1.1.2 (Dec 2018) and warned for 6+
  years. Migration: rename the keyword.
- `solvers.Pseudo`: removed the deprecated implementation methods
  `_solve_ising_deprecated`, `cond_log_likelihood`, `cond_jac`,
  `cond_hess`, `pair_cooc_mat`, `pseudo_log_likelihood`. These were
  superseded by the standard algorithm introduced in v2.1.0
  (Nov 2019).
- `enumerate._write_matlab`: removed. Dead since it was added
  (no in-tree callers; the docstring already said "DEPRECATED:
  code here for future referencing").
- `from coniii import *` no longer re-exports `np`, `jit`, `njit`,
  `warn`, `ALPHNUM`, `NUMERALS`, `combinations`, `binom`,
  `multinomial`, `squareform`. Import them directly from their
  source modules.

Moved
~~~~~
- `coniii.mean_field_ising` → `coniii.legacy.mean_field_ising`.
  Direct imports emit a `DeprecationWarning`. Used internally by
  `ClusterExpansion` and `RegularizedMeanField` (silently).
- `coniii.pseudo_inverse_ising` → `coniii.legacy.pseudo_inverse_ising`.
  Direct imports emit a `DeprecationWarning`. Not wrapped by any
  solver class.
- `samplers.SWIsing`, `samplers.HamiltonianMC`,
  `samplers.Heisenberg3DSampler` → `coniii.experimental.samplers`.
  These had been raising `NotImplementedError` on construction and
  are kept out of the top-level namespace until validated.

Other
~~~~~
- Build modernized: real `pyproject.toml` (PEP 517/518), slimmer
  `setup.py` that only declares the optional Boost C++ extension.
  Boost is now optional in CI and on systems without conda.
- GitHub Actions CI runs pytest on push to dev/py3.
- Each public module now declares an explicit `__all__`. The names
  available via `from coniii import *` are now a curated 39 instead
  of 55 wildcard re-exports.
- Internal: `calc_e` numba signature was relaxed from
  `int64[:,:]` to accept any integer width; this unblocks MCH on
  systems where the Boost C++ extension is not compiled.
- Internal: dozens of `scipy.X` aliases that scipy 2.0 will remove
  were replaced with their `numpy.X` equivalents.
- `coniii.utils` is now a package split into focused submodules
  (`_indexing`, `_correlations`, `_params`, `_graph`). The public
  API is unchanged.
- Every module now has a proper module-level docstring.
- Docs: README has a new "Package layout" table flagging
  stable/experimental/legacy modules; documentation links now point
  to https://coniii.readthedocs.io. The stale `pypi_description`
  file was removed (README is the PyPI long description).


